The Iron Lady is a 2011 biographical drama film based on the life and career of Margaret Thatcher, a British politician who was the
longest-serving Prime Minister of the United Kingdom of the 20th century and the first woman to hold the office.

11
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
The film was directed by Phyllida Lloyd and written by Abi Morgan.

12
00:57:16,363 --> 00:57:22,363
Thatcher is portrayed primarily by Meryl Streep, and, in her
formative and early political years, by Alexandra Roach.

13
01:02:02,727 --> 01:02:08,727
Thatcher's husband, Denis Thatcher, is portrayed by Jim
Broadbent and by Harry Lloyd as the younger Denis.

14
01:06:49,090 --> 01:06:55,090
Thatcher's longest-serving cabinet member and eventual deputy,
Geoffrey Howe, is portrayed by Anthony Head.

15
01:11:35,454 --> 01:11:41,454
Despite the film's mixed reception, Streep's performance was widely acclaimed.

16
01:16:21,818 --> 01:16:27,818
She received her 17th Oscar nomination for her portrayal and ultimately won the
award for the third time—29 years after her second Oscar win.

17
01:21:08,181 --> 01:21:14,181
She also earned her third Golden Globe Award for Best Actress – Motion Picture Drama award (her eighth
Golden Globe Award win overall) and her second BAFTA Award for Best Actress in a Leading Role.

18
01:25:54,545 --> 01:26:00,545
The film also won the Academy Award for Best Makeup and
the BAFTA Award for Best Makeup and Hair.

19
01:30:40,909 --> 01:30:46,909
The film was loosely based on John Campbell's biography The Iron Lady:
Margaret Thatcher, from Grocer's Daughter to Prime Minister.

20
